# Goal 6: Fix `cprojf` infinity projection

## Function
`cprojf` (complex float projection onto Riemann sphere)

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexf/cprojf.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s6/src/complexf.rs` (around line 120, `cprojf`)

## Problem
MISMATCH — 4 test failures. Same bug pattern as `cproj` (Goal 5) but in the float version.

```
C:    cprojf inff+1i  = inf+0x0p+0i
Rust: cprojf inff+1i  = inf+0x1p+0i

C:    cprojf inff-1i  = inf+-0x0p+0i
Rust: cprojf inff-1i  = inf+0x1p+0i

C:    cprojf inf+1i   = inf+0x0p+0i
Rust: cprojf inf+1i   = inf+0x1p+0i
```

## What Needs to Change
Same fix as Goal 5: when either component is infinite, return `INFINITY + copysign(0.0, imag)`. The float version has the same missing infinity-projection logic.

## Success Criteria
- `cprojf(inff+1i)` = `inf+0x0p+0i` (bitwise match)
- `cprojf(inff-1i)` = `inf+-0x0p+0i` (bitwise match, signed zero)
- All 4 failing tests pass with bitwise-exact match
